.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt BSDBT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsdbt
.Nd list, find, pair and remove Bluetooth devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar adapter
.Op Cm list
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar adapter
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Cm scan
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar adapter
.Op Fl k | Fl p Ar pin
.Cm pair Ar address
.Nm
.Cm remove Ar address
.Nm
.Cm disconnect Ar address
.Nm
.Fl a Ar device
.Cm power Cm on | off
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility manages Bluetooth devices with the
.Fx
Bluetooth stack and its daemons
.Xr hcsecd 8
(pairing, link keys) and
.Xr bthidd 8
(keyboards and mice).
It does the same as the XFCE panel plugin
.Nm xfce4-bsdbluetooth-plugin .
.Pp
.Cm list
and
.Cm scan
run as an ordinary user: they talk to the adapter directly through an HCI
socket, see
.Xr ng_hci 4
and
.Xr bluetooth 3 .
The other commands change the system and run
.Xr bsdbt-helper 8
through
.Xr pkexec 1 ;
polkit allows that to the user at the console without a password.
Run as root,
.Nm
calls the helper directly.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-a adapter"
.It Fl a Ar adapter
The adapter, by HCI node
.Pq Dq ubt0hci
or device
.Pq Dq ubt0 .
Without it,
.Nm
uses the first adapter that is up.
.It Fl k
Pair a keyboard:
.Nm
makes up a six-digit PIN and prints it, to be typed on the keyboard
followed by Enter while pairing.
.It Fl p Ar pin
The PIN of the device, from its manual.
Without
.Fl k
or
.Fl p ,
the PIN is 0000, which most mice and headsets use.
.It Fl t Ar seconds
How long
.Cm scan
looks for devices, 1 to 60 seconds; 10 by default.
.El
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width disconnect
.It Cm list
The adapters with their address, name, class, scan mode and open
connections, and the devices set up with
.Nm ,
paired or not, connected or not.
This is the default.
.It Cm scan
Look for devices in range that can be discovered (a device usually has
to be put in pairing mode) and print their address, kind and name.
.It Cm pair
Pair with the device, keep its link key so that it reconnects after a
reboot, and if it is a keyboard, mouse or other input device, set it up
for
.Xr bthidd 8 ,
which then connects to it.
.It Cm remove
Forget the device: its link key and its entries for
.Xr hcsecd 8
and
.Xr bthidd 8 .
.It Cm disconnect
Close the connection to the device.
An input device connects again when it is used.
.It Cm power
Start or stop the Bluetooth stack on
.Ar device
.Pq Dq service bluetooth start ubt0 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/db/bsdbt.devices -compact
.It Pa /var/db/bsdbt.devices
the devices set up with
.Nm ,
written by
.Xr bsdbt-helper 8
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 for a usage error, 4 when the device refused
to pair (wrong PIN), 5 when it did not answer.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find a mouse in pairing mode and pair it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ bsdbt scan
00:11:22:33:44:55  mouse           Bluetooth Mouse
$ bsdbt pair 00:11:22:33:44:55
.Ed
.Pp
Pair a keyboard:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ bsdbt -k pair 00:11:22:33:44:66
Type 482913 on the keyboard, then press Enter.
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr bluetooth 3 ,
.Xr ng_hci 4 ,
.Xr bsdbt-helper 8 ,
.Xr bthidd 8 ,
.Xr hcsecd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An wugq Aq Mt wugq.dev@gmail.com
.Sh BUGS
Only Bluetooth Classic devices work; the
.Fx
stack has no Bluetooth Low Energy input devices.
.Xr hcsecd 8
has no Secure Simple Pairing, so a device that refuses legacy PIN
pairing cannot be paired.
